       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the labeled maximum daily dose of 10 mg for adults. A dose that high risks severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that limit.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Possible typo:** If you meant 5 mg once daily (the usual starting dose) or 10 mg once daily (the maximum), I can enter either one right away.\n- **Inadequate BP control:** Amlodipine is capped at 10 mg/day, so the usual next step is to add a second agent, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide-like diuretic. I can enter that order if you tell me the drug and dose.\n- **Overdose or other intent:** If this isn't meant to be a standard therapeutic order, it should go through toxicology or pharmacy and not routine order entry.\n\nWhich would you like me to do?"
