       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note. Even if both are accurate, I'm not able to enter a dose above the labeled maximum daily dose of 10 mg. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is five times that limit.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Enter a dose within the label now.** I can enter amlodipine 10 mg by mouth once daily, or 5 mg if you want to titrate. Just tell me which.\n- **Add a second agent.** If standard dosing failed, combination therapy is the usual route. I can enter an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide-like diuretic at a dose you specify.\n- **Use pharmacy.** If the specialist really wants an off-label dose, the pharmacy or the specialist can enter or co-sign it through the hospital's non-standard dose process. That process usually includes a documented rationale, monitoring parameters, and a pharmacist review. I can't bypass that safeguard from here.\n\nWould you like me to enter any of the within-label options?"
      }
